      "hints": [
        "Set $a + 0.5b = 4$ and $a + b = 3$.",
        "Solve simultaneously to get $a = 5, b = -2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the given values to set up simultaneous linear equations for $f(x) = a + b\\sin x$:\n$$f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = a + b\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = a + \\frac{1}{2}b = 4$$\n$$f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = a + b\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = a + b = 3$$",
        "Subtract the first equation from the second:\n$$\\frac{1}{2}b = -1 \\implies b = -2$$\n$$a = 3 - (-2) = 5$$\n$$a = 5, \\quad b = -2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Simultaneous Equations": "Forms $a + 0.5b = 4$ and $a + b = 3$ (M1). Solves for $a = 5$ (A1) and $b = -2$ (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
