      "hints": [
        "Set $c + |d| = 10$ and $c - |d| = -4$.",
        "Solve to find $c = 3$ and $d = 7$ (or $d = -7$)."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "For $g(x) = c + d\\sin x$, the range $[-4, 10]$ is determined by the minimum and maximum of the sine function:\n$$\\text{Maximum: } c + |d| = 10$$\n$$\\text{Minimum: } c - |d| = -4$$",
        "Solve for the vertical translation $c$ and amplitude $|d|$:\n$$2c = 6 \\implies c = 3$$\n$$|d| = 10 - 3 = 7 \\implies d = 7 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad d = -7$$\n$$c = 3, \\quad d = 7 \\quad (\\text{or } d = -7)$$"
      ],
